# HTTPS front end for SirisOS, the same pattern as SirisAI's (caddy/Caddyfile
# in bradmairs/SirisAI): a self-signed certificate (tls internal) because
# SirisOS stays on the LAN. Browsers only allow the microphone on a secure
# page, so the Siris voice orb needs this; plain http on SIRISOS_PORT keeps
# working for everything else.
#
# The first visit from each device shows a certificate warning: accept it
# once. default_sni is needed because devices reach this by bare IP, and
# TLS sends no server name for an IP address.
{
	default_sni 192.168.0.100
}

192.168.0.100:8444, localhost:8444 {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy sirisos:6464
}
